            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "Today (Monday, **August 3, 2026**), the most notable “Azure AI–adjacent” news items I can verify are:\n\n- **ArcelorMittal expands its partnership with Microsoft to accelerate AI-led transformation**, including deepening use of **Microsoft Cloud/Azure** and AI capabilities across its operations. ([manilatimes.net](https://www.manilatimes.net/2026/08/03/tmt-newswire/globenewswire/arcelormittal-reshaping-digital-backbone-with-microsoft-cloud-and-ai/2396730))  \n- If you mean “Azure AI product/service updates” specifically (new previews/GA features), the most authoritative place to check **what shipped today** is **Azure Updates** (Microsoft’s official changelog). ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/updates/))  \n- For “Azure AI / Foundry” platform news and posts, the **Azure AI tag** on the Microsoft Azure Blog is the canonical feed for recent writeups and announcements. ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/blog/tag/ai/))  \n\nIf you tell me what you mean by “Azure AI” (e.g., **Azure AI Foundry**, **Azure OpenAI**, **Azure AI Search**, **Document Intelligence**, etc.), I can narrow this down to just *product* announcements/releases rather than customer stories and broader Microsoft-AI news.",
